lossus of Rhodes was traditionally associated with the island\'s harbor, but the familiar image of ships passing between its legs is likely a later myth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-73b9-9bb2-95e5ecf09f98","description":"The Colossus of Rhodes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7bd1-8dda-dcf629507e65","description":"The Temple of Artemis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7453-aeb2-ae42bfab0c91","description":"The Great Pyramid of Giza","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7e60-9da2-b536b20497f6","description":"The Statue of Zeus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7680-8a8a-d2edf87a5870","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What resin was used by Ancient Romans as jewelry?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ancient Romans prized amber jewelry, and trade routes brought much of the material south from the Baltic region.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7d45-8298-027beef3bd8d","description":"Amber","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-73d0-ab67-566e24f6f64e","description":"Acacia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-78be-9ddd-a4e1bb93590a","description":"Carob","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-761f-9867-0691b8398d8f","description":"Bees Wax","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7b84-ac42-38cdc14f9351","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Victorian engineer designed the Great Western Railway?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Isambard Kingdom Brunel also designed the SS Great Britain, an iron-hulled steamship now preserved in Bristol.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-737f-b4ef-2126d392e5d3","description":"Isambard Kingdom Brunel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7d04-8c8a-cb2988d47d7b","description":"Robert Stephenson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-7047-beca-2677a9236e7a","description":"Thomas Telford","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f2-73ef-82d8-c689a0e5