ountries was founded during the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The United States adopted the Declaration of Independence in 1776, and its Constitution took effect in 1789.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7405-a5bd-615b4f0e0781","description":"The United States of America","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7035-8cbb-42cc040ec81a","description":"Canada","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c5c-872d-06a0cfeb7873","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7306-ba1d-aa4d496190ac","description":"India","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7dc9-95f0-685fa4c4e7f7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was Byzantium renamed in AD 330?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Constantinople was named for Emperor Constantine the Great and became the eastern Roman Empire\u2019s capital.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7823-a864-e17cb0c65882","description":"Constantinople","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7cc7-bdd6-71d3616ca1c5","description":"Antioch","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7904-9d13-957136311ddd","description":"Nicaea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-787c-ac1a-902351898a09","description":"Alexandria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7209-8d13-e59e40968e4e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What man-made waterway did the 1979 Israel-Egypt Peace Treaty allow Israel access to?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Suez Canal is a major shipping route between Europe and Asia, avoiding the much longer trip around Africa.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-77f4-899b-f4f736c8caef","description":"The Suez Canal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-799d-9aea-a46d5a175639","description":"The Panama Canal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7666-921b-11ce5e309476","description":"The Kiel Canal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f81-a41a-