nce of the Russian imperial family.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73eb-818c-e4185782259c","description":"Yalta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7fc9-b1a6-b8f79d3a7588","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7333-a520-a2221232601c","description":"Maastricht","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7e2c-abda-b6a332bb855c","description":"Versailles","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7fd6-b37c-e2fd5cb80f05","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What is the Roman numeral for fifty?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"L represents 50; XL is 40 and LX is 60, using subtraction and addition around it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-79e3-b68c-f890996efa12","description":"L","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7858-8a31-00d074ddb536","description":"R","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7524-ad77-7e586c75718b","description":"H","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a04-9171-80f5092f62d8","description":"J","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72ad-8ba0-a420b36ebee0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What type of people were obsessed with turning ordinary metals into gold in the Middle Ages?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alchemists pursued the philosopher\u2019s stone, and some also believed it could help create an elixir of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7515-8c01-be4d68dab329","description":"Alchemists","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7352-b0dc-125d179b9246","description":"Hussars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-78d9-946d-76eeb8b29789","description":"Chandlers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a69-907e-dea06b97ec08","description":"Smelters","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73dc-a9fb-c84a638a23ac","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese dynasty sent the envoy Zhang Qian west to Central Asia around 138 BC?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Han dynasty sent Zhang Qian during Emperor Wu\u2019s reign. His reports and contacts helped spur trade along routes later known as the Silk Road.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72a6-b339-6b870f0e5f53","description":"Han dynasty","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7487-a205-8767f1140c5b","description":"Tang dynasty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7fce-8b6d-b5c2062081cd","description":"Ming dynasty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72f2-a32c-51836025ff8c","description":"Qin dynasty","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7502-aede-6b8c9d8d7dbd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Shakespearean king was actually king of Scotland for 17 years?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Macbeth ruled from 1040 until his death in 1057; Shakespeare\u2019s play took liberties with the historical king\u2019s story.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-77e9-99e1-e1613643cee7","description":"Macbeth","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7600-a46e-8dc0ec87fc90","description":"Lear","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7848-860b-6f9cb58ac391","description":"Hamlet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7909-9df7-a173c0ee07ac","description":"Richard III","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7305-b89c-2d425e4c2fd7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"How many colonies signed the American Declaration of Independence?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Thirteen colonies signed the Declaration; they later became the original states of the United States.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7883-a575-9b78fcdad01b","description":"13","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7123-9d8a-ed2c7a7b87c1","description":"9","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-798e-bcd1-da708c5a2255","description":"15","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c8e-ad9d-e7d81028de28","description":"50","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f8c-8e05-9146266c7079","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which French city did Joan of Arc relieve from an English siege?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Orleans was relieved in 1429, a major French success in the Hundred Years\u2019 War that helped restore momentum to Charles VII\u2019s cause.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b93-b472-69d862c86dd2","description":"Orleans","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7009-b819-084e5e4591ca","description":"Reims","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a4d-b047-642d7fed90df","description":"Rouen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-708b-940d-a53bbcd26aee","description":"Paris","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-700b-9517-f99f0a5fee86","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Before becoming a politician, which US President was a Hollywood actor?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ronald Reagan later served as president of the Screen Actors Guild before entering politics.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7673-87b2-e05e3162865b","description":"Ronald Reagan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73b0-86e4-8da86bd8736e","description":"John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7ebe-9e4a-2823d9175735","description":"Abraham Lincoln","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7325-9e28-e4135abd7c6b","description":"Barack Obama","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c73-ba7f-9ffb4d68a59a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Cold War between the U.S. and Soviet Union begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1947 is often used as the starting point because the Truman Doctrine formalized U.S. opposition to the spread of communism, though the Cold War developed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f89-86ce-c990d458921f","description":"1947","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c22-b18d-ff38a6d7193a","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7480-9a35-83768d63bcc4","description":"1938","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7bd1-9ff6-bc6544eed2e8","description":"1955","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-75c5-b607-d044f7c6717d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the last president of the Soviet Union?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mikhail Gorbachev was the Soviet Union\u2019s first and only president; the office ended when the country dissolved in 1991.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7ce8-9c4b-2369021d752f","description":"Gorbachev","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-792a-9fbc-cc24c34ac4c3","description":"Yeltsin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-702a-b4e9-b4b87113559c","description":"Putin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7e2e-aa06-2e6708662898","description":"Khrushchev","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-756d-acce-32f312683b40","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who wrote a famous diary between 1660 and 1669?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Samuel Pepys wrote much of his diary in shorthand, and it was not fully published until long after his death.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7ed8-b9fd-0761b2c6c044","description":"Samuel Pepys","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-74b3-b4f9-c71f353280d6","description":"Anne Frank","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a6e-a8ca-3b5a7c1c75a0","description":"Samuel Johnson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-76a8-a457-abebdf2548f2","description":"Daniel Defoe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7866-be86-88b1f9e48661","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the name of the prominent religious conflict that arose in Europe in the 17th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Thirty Years\' War ended with the Peace of Westphalia in 1648, a settlement that reshaped the political map of Central Europe.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-71c7-bc59-4e736783ace8","description":"The Thirty Years\' War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7dbb-9133-9e0ed81d84f1","description":"The Hundred Years\' War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b97-9ec8-3f8bd13c3d42","description":"The War of the Roses","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-79ae-84f1-ec4b8c62676a","description":"The War of Spanish Succession","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7575-b54e-ffa2b55e17d6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Germany\'s allies in World War I were Austria-Hungary, Bulgaria and which other state?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Ottoman Empire joined the Central Powers in 1914 and fought Allied forces at Gallipoli and across the Middle East.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-74f2-8ca4-ab1d4365cd57","description":"The Ottoman Empire","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7452-9833-131e512bfb18","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7309-90e1-d0261d2c5c23","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7703-83a3-2ded17514a6a","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-735d-ac16-e64a2beb8628","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What war was the USA involved in between 1950 and 1953?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Korean War ended in an armistice in 1953, not a formal peace treaty, so the peninsula remains divided.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c9c-b77e-db2789c99a59","description":"Korean War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7835-bc65-5fce654e43a7","description":"Vietnam War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-78a1-a77a-2634015214e1","description":"World War I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-70ec-a3aa-d99a6fffb55f","description":"World War II","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72b1-8e02-5fbbd8efa1a7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the nickname given to the possible computer bug that caused worldwide concern leading up to the year 2000?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Y2K concerns centered on whether software using two-digit years would treat \u201c00\u201d as 1900 instead of 2000, potentially disrupting computer systems.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-77a5-b745-e9e0ed6eda13","description":"Y2K","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-79cd-b299-c3b11296a258","description":"Bug2000","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-731d-8c18-bf5a40d5353b","description":"Trojan Horse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7369-b264-6a476b4644d7","description":"The Millennial Worm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7727-a1e1-6e5bd1f6a8af","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which country was Adolf Hitler born?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Adolf Hitler was born in Braunau am Inn, Austria, in 1889, when the country was part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7401-9682-47928fa05a7a","description":"Austria","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-78d4-ad02-3719e3bec625","description":"Germany","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7400-85f4-ea3d36c69685","description":"Belgium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7efe-b6f7-288aebfb0a5a","description":"Switzerland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-77f6-ba1f-7945060b9112","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which French king was married to Marie Antoinette?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Louis XVI was executed by guillotine in 1793; Marie Antoinette was executed later that year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7cc0-a587-283aff8306c3","description":"Louis XVI","cor