9-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"King Ancus Marcius is said to have built the Sublician Bridge, the first bridge across which river in the 7th century B.C.?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Tiber runs through Rome, and the Sublician Bridge became famous in Roman legend for Horatius Cocles\'s stand against an invading army.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7d78-a2a3-d74e85f4006d","description":"The Tiber","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7601-8412-d874698e37b3","description":"The Nile","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-75f8-a674-cfc352287eb7","description":"The Thames","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c51-8ca1-054deafcfa62","description":"The Seine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-762f-8bb0-664e288d7c25","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What year did World War II begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1939 is the year Germany invaded Poland on September 1; Britain and France declared war two days later.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7efd-9b9f-cba7590abf3a","description":"1939","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7e37-a961-6fec4919d184","description":"1941","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-74a6-bc91-1c1f1adc8df6","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-77a2-8bc6-4e46dcca6aa9","description":"1937","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7bd7-9a0c-a32f8fba2481","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which World War I battle is remembered for the Parisian taxicabs that ferried French troops to the front line in 1914?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The French victory at the Marne halted the German advance toward Paris and helped set the Western Front into a prolonged stalemate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72d3-a81b-45a1f8048099","description":"Battle of the Marne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73e4-a699-6b3dd91ca10b","description":"Battle of the Somme","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7da2-bf30-dc64e65c2d4e","description":"Battle of Ypres","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-714c-8168-456591ddac29","description":"Battle of Verdun","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a22-bb2d-ba88f6835b03","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the major economic revolution that started in the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain and reshaped manufacturing as production shifted toward machinery and factories.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-70c4-b0db-1711b9c4cd02","description":"The Industrial Revolution","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7edd-81e7-a7bfba0febda","description":"The French Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-79c3-8b55-c3c80be80f75","description":"The American Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72f9-97eb-823f7e426677","description":"The Enlightenment","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7ab4-8b11-5a5be374884c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What group of ships, commanded by the Duke of Medina, was considered invincible but was defeated by The Royal Navy in 1588?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Spanish Armada was disrupted by English fireships, and storms battered many ships as they retreated around Scotland and Ireland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-766a-a9a5-5a0d3e3b4e03","description":"Spanish Armada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7bbf-a4c2-e6c2b85323c4","description":"The Napoleonic Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-752c-8af7-c91caa24afd3","description":"The Viking Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7db0-a5ad-f27e0729dec3","description":"The Scottish Armada","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7758-9014-46d9293508f6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the second man to walk on the Moon, after Neil Armstrong?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Buzz Aldrin and Neil Armstrong landed together while Michael Collins remained aboard the command module in lunar orbit.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-706b-a9b6-59d913519c3f","description":"Buzz Aldrin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73cc-8cb8-4fc6e0940349","description":"Yuri Gagarin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7cd1-b134-d261d1a534f5","description":"Alan Shepard","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f3b-af0e-543941c5bd23","description":"James Irwin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-718c-9f54-64fa82fa0841","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What kind of government dominated most of Europe during the 17th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Absolute monarchs centralized authority over government, taxation, and the military. Louis XIV of France is one of the best-known examples.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-70cf-afde-ba097bcc149a","description":"Absolute Monarchy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7394-99f5-118cc8e176eb","description":"Democracy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7867-99df-03d0f071a1e7","description":"Constitutional Monarchy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-76b1-afed-01ee9898d4da","description":"Parliamentary Democracy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7942-9011-bc9bc422d629","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What city was destroyed by a \'little boy\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hiroshima was struck by the first atomic bomb used in warfare, dropped by the U.S. B-29 Enola Gay in August 1945.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73e1-b0bf-f60590959742","description":"Hiroshima","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-74bb-bcf1-0efdce834a4b","description":"Jericho","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f5d-85ae-c0f0a8a37220","description":"Babel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-79ec-8648-716981bd229b","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-715a-b85e-3a45195af2a8","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What age preceded the Iron Age?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, and its widespread use gave this period its name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b96-96cd-062ab41f1379","description":"The Bronze Age","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7d3b-8874-e22488b37249","description":"The Stone Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7880-a5a6-260ab54c5a54","description":"The Steel Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7992-bf05-cc45553761c7","description":"The Wooden Age","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-74fc-93ac-7c06d9123c05","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What notorious event occurred on the 24th October 1929?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Wall Street Crash began with Black Thursday, as investors rushed to sell shares. The market turmoil helped usher in the Great Depression.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7c3f-8505-9ac3d1964ce7","description":"The Wall Street Crash","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7cc0-8b28-125294c291ef","description":"The Hindenberg Disaster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7d9f-b4c8-4449c4c3c66b","description":"The Assassination of John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7fae-9bc3-32dcecac6fef","description":"The Nazi Invasion of Poland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7677-8d84-dbad93af296e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1945, which German city hosted the trials where former Nazi leaders were prosecuted for war crimes?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The proceedings became known as the Nuremberg Trials and helped establish that political and military leaders could be held individually responsible for international crimes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-73cb-9b55-6cd3df501b39","description":"Nuremberg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7d72-99d4-ad78f59e8753","description":"Berlin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7070-9faf-c2c05fff8ad6","description":"Munich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7806-946e-f1354f7773f2","description":"Frankfurt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-747b-8bac-de8660e1dc47","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the term used for a pirate who was licensed by the crown to capture enemy ships and cargo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A privateer operated under a letter of marque, making attacks on enemy vessels lawful for the crown; pirates acted without that authorization.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-740b-a369-327d04c97451","description":"A privateer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-734f-b444-59617d9f6e23","description":"A smuggler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-790f-bebc-c0efc0669330","description":"A mutineer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f2a-89b5-3772e3385e9a","description":"A sea wolf","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-76c2-b9b4-9b24da1ba0c7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which American gangster was shot dead outside a Chicago cinema in July 1934?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"John Dillinger was shot by FBI agents outside Chicago\'s Biograph Theater on 22 July 1934.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-710b-9f87-e5341278a987","description":"John Dillinger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f46-bc7d-97578a473eb7","description":"Al Capone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-701e-8d2a-84ab2bec2014","description":"Vito Corleone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b0b-b299-5f1639bdb92f","description":"Ronald Kray","correct_answer":f