ion":"What mountain range did Hannibal march through in 218 B.C.?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hannibal crossed the Alps during the Second Punic War with an army that famously included war elephants.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f33-97b9-c8825c627ceb","description":"The Alps","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-72e3-aef8-c27bf23c1ac6","description":"The Pindus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a4a-add5-1b7170c99662","description":"The Atlas Mountains","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-761e-a1a9-ef71d59a5248","description":"The Urals","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7f58-8fa6-c1062ad60303","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Where did the bayonet originate?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The bayonet is named for Bayonne, where early versions are traditionally said to have originated, though the weapon\u2019s precise beginnings are debated.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7dd5-b117-605929653ce0","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7534-9a0c-3c4e33b42fdb","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7dcb-afe1-7c97ba326557","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7a76-90c5-0e01fff3e412","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7738-9ffd-d243e0eed8f2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the name of the son of Cleopatra & Julius Caesar?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Caesarion was also known as Ptolemy XV and was presented by Cleopatra as Julius Caesar\u2019s heir.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7101-b976-fc3fad723491","description":"Caesarion","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b8e-936b-3fb257878f33","description":"Octavian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7d84-87fe-cdb67df4cc77","description":"Augustus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36f4-7b08-82f1-55da4dd166c6","desc